# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_sibling_symbol_probe.py" "SIBLING SYMBOL GATE: PASS" "sibling-symbol probe (shared specific token as sibling-coupling recovery — measure-first, honest near-NO)" "sibling-symbol probe: a MEASURE-FIRST probe asking whether a SHARED SPECIFIC STRING/IDENTIFIER (an event name, DI/registry key, feature-flag, action-type, queue name) can recover the AI-era sibling-module coupling the single-language code graph misses (PR #268: ~61% of missed coupling is same-language, cross-dir, no graph edge). MEASURED on the AI-era panel (10 real indie repos, python/ts/go): shared-SPECIFIC-token same-lang cross-dir no-edge pairs DO co-change ~5-6x above random same-lang cross-dir pairs, consistently across ALL repos -- so the LIFT is real. BUT precision is the blocker: even after the strongest specificity filter (drop ubiquitous tokens + CSS-utility classes + import specifiers + date/format/stdlib constants), ~44% of shared tokens are still INCIDENTAL (icon names, generic snake_case, format constants) that share by convention not by contract, and no structural filter cleanly separates a real contract from an incidental structured string. HONEST VERDICT = QUALIFIED: a real but noise-prone signal, viable ONLY as a low-weight ADVISORY hint stacked on co-change, NEVER a shippable standalone detector -- a measured near-NO, the intended result. This gate proves the harness LOGIC deterministically with NO network/clone/Postgres: (1) the specificity filter is precision-safe -- rejects common/prose strings ('error'/'true'/'GET'/'id'/'a sentence'), keeps real contracts ('user.created'/'ENABLE_BILLING'/'orders/ADD_ITEM'), and the CLEAN mode additionally removes the measured noise classes (the specificity-filter effect is a real delta, not a no-op, while a genuine contract token survives); (2) on a built code graph + temp git repo the candidate definition is correct -- a pair is emitted ONLY when same-language + cross-dir + shares a surviving specific token + has NO structural graph edge (a same-token pair WITH an import edge is excluded, edge-absence is enforced and non-vacuous); (3) the lift metric matches backtest_cochange ((#co-change*T)/(n_a*n_b)) and ranks a tightly co-changing sibling pair above a loosely-overlapping one; (4) CONTENT-FREE EGRESS is enforced -- _tokens_of returns ONLY a set of short token strings, never a file body (proven on a temp file whose secret body line must NOT appear in the returned tokens), and the co-change scan uses git --name-only + %H ONLY, never commit bodies/diffs (%b/-p/--patch/--name-status); (5) the honest verdict is structurally protected -- the verdict logic classifies the measured real-lift-but-noisy (44%-FP) outcome as QUALIFIED/not-shippable-standalone and can reach SHIP-CANDIDATE only at clean (<=25% FP) precision, so the measure-first NO can never be silently flipped to a clean YES" "sibling-symbol probe: shared SPECIFIC tokens co-change ~5-6x above random (real lift, all repos) BUT ~44% incidental even after the strongest specificity filter => QUALIFIED advisory signal, NOT a shippable standalone detector (honest measured near-NO); harness proven precision-safe, edge-absent, content-free (tokens+paths only, no bodies, git --name-only/%H), verdict-honest (real-but-noisy => QUALIFIED, never a silent SHIP)" 24
